# ============================================================================
# 05_ WGCNA module detection + ASPC/NEPC module-trait association — v3
# ============================================================================
# Consumes the bulk cohort plus single-cell evidence from 02_/03_, and writes
# the module-membership table 06_ integrates.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ERROR THAT MOTIVATED v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Error: unable to find an inherited method for function 'select'
#          for signature 'x = "tbl_df"'
#
# `select` resolved to AnnotationDbi::select(), an S4 generic with no tbl_df
# method. edgeR attaches AnnotationDbi transitively, and it loads after dplyr,
# so it wins the search path. Identical to the failure in 04_ v2, and to the
# MASS::select failure in 06_ v4.
#
# Load order is not a durable fix — it breaks again whenever a dependency
# changes what it attaches. v3 namespace-qualifies EVERY dplyr verb, plus
# stats::sd / var / median / cor / hclust / dist / p.adjust. WGCNA additionally
# masks cor and dist, so those two matter here even more than in 04_.
#
# Step 9 is where v2 died, so Steps 1-8 completed: the network was built. The
# module-trait association, membership table and every CSV 06_ reads were NOT
# written. Nothing downstream of this script has valid v2 output.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CARRIED FORWARD FROM v2 — BOTH SUBSTANTIVE FIXES INTACT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. ASPC_fraction EXCLUDED FROM RESIDUALISATION.
#    v1 regressed it out of the matrix before module detection, which removes
#    any ASPC-driven module by construction. The surviving modules could not
#    be ASPC modules, so 06_'s in_wgcna_module could not carry the meaning it
#    was given. Same decision as 04_: never residualise on a target.
#
# 2. MODULE-TRAIT STEP EXISTS.
#    v1 set in_wgcna_module TRUE for any gene in any non-grey module with
#    |kME| >= 0.30 — about half the genes in a typical run. That is evidence
#    of being co-expressed with something, not of ASPC association. v3 keeps
#    the permissive definition as in_any_module and restricts in_wgcna_module
#    to modules that actually correlate with ASPC_fraction.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEW IN v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * GREY IS REPORTED, NEVER SELECTED. Grey is the UNASSIGNED bin, not a
#     module — its eigengene is the first PC of genes that failed to cluster.
#     A strong grey-trait correlation means real structure was missed, usually
#     because the power fragmented a genuine module. A previous run had grey
#     correlating 0.745 with NEPC_score, the second strongest association in
#     the table; that is a warning about the network, not a finding.
#   * ALL PLOTTING WRAPPED. safe_plot() means a graphics failure cannot abort
#     the run, and every CSV 06_ depends on is written before plotting.
#   * FALLBACK MODULE IS FLAGGED. When no module clears FDR and |r|, v2 fell
#     back to the single best-correlated module silently. v3 records
#     aspc_selection_mode in the summary and provenance, so a fallback module
#     is never mistaken for a significant one.
#   * COLLINEARITY CHECK. If cor(ASPC_fraction, stromal_fraction) is high, an
#     "ASPC module" is really a stromal module; residualising on stromal
#     content also strips the variance the ASPC trait needs. Reported before
#     module detection.
#   * SAMPLE-ID DIAGNOSTIC on the covariate join, since a silent zero-overlap
#     here is the same failure mode that gave 06_ zero survival samples.
#   * Ratio column accepts target_specific_ratio (03_ v6) or the legacy
#     aspc_specific_ratio.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCOPE — WHAT MODULE MEMBERSHIP MEANS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is BULK co-expression. A gene in the ASPC module co-varies with ASPC
# content ACROSS PATIENTS, which reflects stromal infiltration, purity and
# treatment as much as any cell-intrinsic programme. It is weaker evidence
# than the single-cell specificity ratio from 03_, and 06_ should weight it
# accordingly.
#
# OUTPUTS (out_dir)
#   wgcna_module_membership.csv   gene, module, kME, in_wgcna_module   <- 06_
#   wgcna_module_trait.csv        module x trait correlation + FDR
#   wgcna_module_summary.csv      size, ASPC r, NEPC r, verdict
#   wgcna_eigengenes.csv          sample x module eigengene values
#   wgcna_result.rds              datExpr, MEs, colours, params
#   wgcna.PROVENANCE.txt
#   *.pdf                         QC, soft threshold, dendrogram, heatmap
# ============================================================================

